{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c50b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a841-0b8e-7df2-8923-843adf19c894"},"sequence":224,"recorded_at":1780531400000443,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a841-9620-7582-994a-0870fc7ca66b"},"task_id":"01a0a841-9620-7582-994a-0870fc7ca66b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a841-9620-7582-994a-0870fc7ca66b","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/outcome-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-97dhxd — rework rev2 outcome (review findings F1–F5)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review` via handoff).\n4|Candidate: uncommitted in Story worktree, branch tip unchanged at `7d2126a`.\n5|\n6|## F1 — session restore from Keychain (was: in-memory only)\n7|\n8|- New `GitHubSessionIdentityStore.swift`: non-secret identity\n9|  (`serverHost`, `userID`, `clientID`, `username`) in UserDefaults;\n10|  tokens stay in Keychain. In-memory store for tests.\n11|- New `GitHubAuth.Effect.restoreSession` + `Action.restoreStarted`\n12|  (reducer → existing `.verifyingAccount`; no UI change needed).\n13|  Flow loads identity → Keychain record → PAT-shape check →\n14|  opportunistic serialized refresh → `GET /user` validation →\n15|  installations (+ first-installation repositories) → `.connected`.\n16|- 401/revoked/`invalid_grant`/PAT-shaped store → clears Keychain +\n17|  identity, `.failed(relogin|none)`. Offline/403/rate-limit →\n18|  restored session with stale `syncFailed`; local control and logout\n19|  stay available. Missing Keychain record clears orphan identity.\n20|- `logout` also deletes identity, and reaches persisted stores via the\n21|  identity when the in-memory session is already gone (relaunch can\n22|  never orphan tokens).\n23|- Production call site: `AppRegistry.start()` dispatches\n24|  `.restoreSession` once after `RunnerRuntime.make`, before the loops,\n25|  so the 30 s GitHub loop sees `.connected`.\n26|- Spec: `.spec/github-login-device-flow.md` gains a Session restore section.\n27|\n28|## F2 — refresh concurrency at the production call site\n29|\n30|`GitHubAuth.Flow.currentToken()` (used by `.refreshInstallations` and\n31|`.selectInstallation`) is now driven directly: expiring token\n32|(`expiresAt` now+30 s) → one refresh POST observed in\n33|`TestTransport.requests` → stored token rotates → `syncSucceeded`;\n34|`invalid_grant` on refresh → `.failed(relogin)`; two concurrent Flow\n35|callers (`refreshInstallations` + `selectInstallation(7)`) coalesce to\n36|exactly one `refresh_token` grant (URL-routing test transport).\n37|\n38|## F3 — PAT guard on the refresh path\n39|\n40|`refreshRejectsFineGrainedPATWithoutSaving` feeds\n41|`{\"access_token\":\"github_pat_...\"}` to `GitHubTokenRefresh.refresh`,\n42|expects `.patNotSupported`, and proves the Keychain still holds the\n43|old `ghu_` token. All three `PATGuard` call sites now have negative tests.\n44|\n45|## F4 — audit wired; redaction bounded\n46|\n47|- `AppConfig.current(bundle:serverHost:)` now calls\n48|  `auditNoSecrets(in: bundle.infoDictionary)` first and fails closed.\n49|  `configAuditRunsThroughCurrentBundle` drives both branches through\n50|  `current(bundle:)` with real temp `.bundle` plists (tainted → \n51|  `.embeddedSecret(\"ClientSecret\")`; clean → loads).\n52|- `Redaction.sanitize` has no production caller: STATED BOUND.\n53|  No diagnostics export exists in this slice (log tail / `_diag`\n54|  lands with catalog/lifecycle); `RuntimeLogger` emits action types\n55|  only, so there is nothing to scrub. Noted in code + here.\n56|\n57|## F5 — public binding embedded via generator\n58|\n59|- `ios-app-manager.json`: `GitHubAppClientID: \"Iv23ligBUam7vZitsE1G\"`,\n60|  `GitHubAppSlug: \"relux-runner-control\"`, `marketing_version: \"1.2.0\"`.\n61|- Regenerated with `/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/work/ios-app-manager generate macos-app`\n62|  (exit 0, \"existing source files preserved\"). `Project.swift` diff is\n63|  exactly: version 1.2.0 + the two public keys. Never hand-edited.\n64|- Release `Info.plist` carries `GitHubAppClientID` /\n65|  `GitHubAppSlug`; plist + binary strings contain no\n66|  `secret`/`private_key`/`ghp_`/`github_pat_`/`ghu_`/`ghr_` material.\n67|  No installation IDs, accounts, users, orgs, or repos hardcoded.\n68|\n69|## Incidental (kept minimal)\n70|\n71|- `handlePollSuccess` split into `loadLoginRepositories` +\n72|  `loginInstallationsFailed` (identical dispatch order) to fix the\n73|  pre-existing `cyclomatic_complexity` lint error (22 → under 20).\n74|- Fixed pre-existing lint errors in touched test files\n75|  (`try!` → `try` / scoped disable, `a`/`b`/`v` renames).\n76|- New test `flowLoginPhase401DuringInstallationsRequiresRelogin`\n77|  closes the login-tail 401 branch the split touched.\n78|\n79|## AC coverage — 9 of 11 rows driven via committed tests\n80|\n81|| # | AC row | Named committed test(s) | Production call site |\n82||---|---|---|---|\n83|| 1 | App builds | BOUND (verified via `./Scripts/build.sh` below, not a unit test) | `tuist generate` → `xcodebuild -scheme RunnerControl` → `codesign --verify` |\n84|| 2 | Real login UI drives production services | `flowLoginSuccessDrivesProductionEffectsToConnected` (+ `flowLoginPersistsSessionIdentityForLaterRestore`; UI binding manual, no UI tests) | `ManagementWindowContainer.beginLogin → GitHubAuth.Effect.beginLogin → GitHubAuth.Flow.apply` |\n85|| 3 | Cancellation | `flowCancellationDestroysCodeAndStopsPoll`, `flowCancelWhileConnectedRestoresConnected` | `GitHubAuth.Flow.apply(.cancelLogin)` |\n86|| 4 | slow_down | `flowSlowDownIncreasesIntervalThenSucceeds`, `slowDownAddsFiveSeconds` | `GitHubDeviceFlow.pollOnce` + `nextInterval` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin)` |\n87|| 5 | Expired code | `flowExpiredCodeFailsWithNewCode` | `GitHubDeviceFlow.pollOnce` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin)` |\n88|| 6 | Refresh concurrency | `flowRefreshInstallationsRefreshesExpiringTokenViaProductionPath`, `flowConcurrentRefreshAndSelectCoalesceToSingleRefresh`, `flowRefreshInstallationsWithInvalidGrantDuringRefreshRequiresRelogin` (+ helper `refreshSavesAtomicallyAndCoalescesConcurrentCallers`) | `GitHubAuth.Flow.currentToken()` via `Flow.apply(.refreshInstallations)` / `.selectInstallation` |\n89|| 7 | Logout (+ F1 restore) | `flowRestoreSessionConnectsFromPersistedIdentityThenLogoutClearsBoth`, `flowRestoreSessionWithRevokedTokenRequiresReloginAndClearsStorage`, `flowRestoreSessionWithoutIdentityIsNoop`, `flowLogoutClearsKeychainAndStopsSync`, `githubReducerRestoreStartedShowsVerifyingAccount` | `GitHubAuth.Flow.apply(.restoreSession)` from `AppRegistry.start()`; `Flow.apply(.logout)` |\n90|| 8 | 401 | `flowLoginPhase401DuringInstallationsRequiresRelogin`, `flow401DuringRefreshRequiresRelogin`, `apiClientMaps401And403` | `GitHubAPIClient.*` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin/.refreshInstallations/.restoreSession)` |\n91|| 9 | 403 | `flow403DuringRefreshKeepsConnectedWithStaleError`, `apiClientMaps401And403` | `GitHubAPIClient.fetchInstallations` via `Flow.apply(.refreshInstallations)` |\n92|| 10 | No PAT fallback | `refreshRejectsFineGrainedPATWithoutSaving`, `patGuardRejectsClassicAndFineGrainedPAT`, `apiClientRefusesPATWithoutNetwork`, `devicePollRejectsPATShapedToken` | `GitHubAuth.PATGuard.validate` via device poll, API client, and token refresh |\n93|| 11 | Existing menu functional | BOUND (Runners suite green; menu UI wiring manual, no UI tests) | `RunnerContainer.change → Runners.Effect.setEnabled → Runners.Flow.apply` |\n94|\n95|## Validation (real exit codes)\n96|\n97|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` → exit 0, 56/56 passed.\n98|- Skill script `run-macos-package-tests.sh --package Packages/RunnerControlCore --output .temp/macos-tests` → exit 0, 56 passed.\n99|- `./Scripts/build.sh` (tuist generate + Release xcodebuild + codesign verify) → exit 0, BUILD SUCCEEDED.\n100|- `codesign --verify --deep --strict .temp/products/RunnerControl.app` → exit 0.\n101|- `swiftlint lint` on 6 touched files → exit 0, 0 serious (118 warnings, same baseline classes as rev1: line_length, trailing_comma).\n102|- Not run: `RUN_LAUNCH_AGENT_INTEGRATION=1` launchd integration (touches host launchd; default suite skips it), UI tests (forbidden), release/notary (other Story).\n103|\n104|## Narrowing mutant evidence, rev2 round (all killed, exit 1)\n105|\n106|| Mutant | Narrowing (what it admits) | Named test that fails | Result |\n107||---|---|---|---|\n108|| R1 (reviewer rerun) Flow refreshes only when `refreshToken == nil` | expiring refreshable token never refreshed | `flowRefreshInstallationsRefreshesExpiringTokenViaProductionPath`, `flowConcurrentRefreshAndSelectCoalesceToSingleRefresh` | KILLED (exit 1; 0 refresh grants, stored token stale, no `syncSucceeded`) |\n109|| R2 (reviewer rerun) refresh-path PAT check is `ghp_`-only | admits `github_pat_*` on refresh | `refreshRejectsFineGrainedPATWithoutSaving` | KILLED (exit 1; mutant saved the PAT, store no longer `ghu_old`) |\n110|| N1 restore 401 narrowed to stale | revoked token restores as connected instead of relogin+clear | `flowRestoreSessionWithRevokedTokenRequiresReloginAndClearsStorage` | KILLED (exit 1; got connected-path actions, not `.failed(relogin)`) |\n111|| N2 logout skips identity delete | identity survives logout | `flowRestoreSessionConnectsFromPersistedIdentityThenLogoutClearsBoth` | KILLED (exit 1; `identities.load() == nil` failed) |\n112|| N3 refresh threshold narrowed to already-expired | admits soon-expiring (now+30 s) without refresh | `flowRefreshInstallationsRefreshesExpiringTokenViaProductionPath` | KILLED (exit 1; 1 token POST not 2, stored token stale) |\n113|| W1 `current(bundle:)` skips audit call | admits embedded `ClientSecret` | `configAuditRunsThroughCurrentBundle` | KILLED (exit 1; admitted secret). Wiring proof; class coverage is M7 (rev1, accepted) |\n114|| L1 login-tail 401 narrowed to `.revoked`-only | login-phase 401 connects instead of relogin | `flowLoginPhase401DuringInstallationsRequiresRelogin` | KILLED (exit 1; got connected-path, not `.failed(relogin)`) |\n115|\n116|Rev1 mutants M1–M8, M9d were accepted by the reviewer (killed); M9/M9c\n117|survivors carry the accepted triple-redundancy bound on untouched\n118|cancellation code — not rerun. No new survivors in rev2.\n119|\n120|## Bounds restated\n121|\n122|- Tokens/`device_code` never in `GitHubAuth.State`, actions, logs, or\n123|  `RuntimeLogger` (type-only). Identity store holds no secrets.\n124|- Offline/403/rate-limit keep local control and the restored session;\n125|  401/revoked → relogin with storage cleared.\n126|- Enterprise hosts get host-scoped endpoints; per-server App\n127|  registration + Device Flow support still required (concrete error).\n128|- No `gh` import, no PAT UI, no client secret/private key anywhere.\n129|- Work left uncommitted in Story worktree; branch tip unchanged.","final_result":true}}}
