ts-rev2.swift`, run in scratch copy): **3 of 3 FAILED against the candidate** — see F6.\n16|\n17|## Rev1 findings — status\n18|\n19|- F1 session restore: RESOLVED. `restoreSession` + identity store + `AppRegistry.start()` dispatch; logout reaches persisted stores via identity. Driven by named Flow tests; N1/N2 kill.\n20|- F2 refresh concurrency at production call site: RESOLVED. `flowRefreshInstallationsRefreshesExpiringTokenViaProductionPath`, `flowConcurrentRefreshAndSelectCoalesceToSingleRefresh`, `flowRefreshInstallationsWithInvalidGrantDuringRefreshRequiresRelogin` drive `Flow.currentToken()`; R1/N3 kill.\n21|- F3 PAT guard on refresh path: RESOLVED. `refreshRejectsFineGrainedPATWithoutSaving`; R2 kills.\n22|- F4 audit wiring: RESOLVED. `AppConfig.current(bundle:)` calls `auditNoSecrets` fail-closed, `configAuditRunsThroughCurrentBundle` drives it; W1 kills. `Redaction.sanitize` stated bound accepted (no diagnostics export in this slice; RuntimeLogger logs action type only).\n23|- F5 public binding: RESOLVED. Verified in composed plist and regen (above).\n24|\n25|## New findings\n26|\n27|### F6 — Logout does not cancel in-flight restore/refresh; restore revives a logged-out session (correctness, blocks acceptance)\n28|Class: \"logout отменяет фоновые операции\" (design §9, additional criteria) / AC row \"logout covered\". `logout()` bumps `generation` and cancels only `pollTask`. `restoreSession()`, `restoreInstallations()`, `refreshInstallations()` and `selectInstallation()` never re-check `generation` (or `session`) after their `await`s, so a logout or a new login that interleaves with a network call is silently undone by the continuation.\n29|\n30|Reproduced with a delaying transport (`SlowTransport`, 150–300 ms), all three fail on the candidate:\n31|- **RA1 `reviewerLogoutDuringRestoreDoesNotReviveSession`**: restore awaiting `/user`, logout arrives. Observed sequence `restoreStarted, loggedOut, accountVerified, installationsLoaded, connected`. After logout the Flow has a live `session`, the identity store is **re-saved** (`identities.load() != nil`), UI shows \"Подключено как @octo\", and a subsequent `refreshInstallations` reaches the network. Keychain tokens are gone, so the next 30 s tick produces \"Session was revoked. Sign in again.\" — the user's logout is reversed and then reported as a revocation.\n32|- **RA2 `reviewerLogoutDuringRefreshDoesNotEmitSyncAfterLoggedOut`**: refresh awaiting `/user/installations`, logout arrives. Observed `…connected, loggedOut, installationsLoaded, syncSucceeded`: installations and `lastSyncAt` repopulate the disconnected state. Realistic window: every 30 s tick × network latency.\n33|- **RA3 `reviewerLoginDuringRestoreIsNotClobberedByRestore`**: user presses \"Войти через GitHub\" while startup restore is in flight; restore's `.connected` lands after `codeReceived` and replaces the device-code screen while the poll keeps running.\n34|\n35|The existing `flowLogoutClearsKeychainAndStopsSync` only checks a refresh dispatched *after* logout (`session == nil` guard) — positive-path for the sequential case; the interleaved class is unchecked.\n36|\n37|Required: capture `generation` at entry of `restoreSession`, `restoreInstallations`, `refreshInstallations`, `selectInstallation` (and `currentToken`), and after every `await` guard `generation == gen` before mutating `session`, saving identity, or dispatching. Add the three attached tests (or equivalents named in the outcome) as committed regression tests, plus one narrowing mutant for this class (e.g. keep the guard in `restoreSession` but drop it only after `fetchUser`, so RA1 must fail). Because this is a first finding of its class, `repeat-of: none`; if it recurs, the next revision must carry the named regression test and mutant per the two-consecutive rule.\n38|\n39|### F7 — \"Lint 0 serious\" does not reproduce (reported-fact finding, secondary)\n40|`swiftlint lint` with the repo's default configuration (no `.swiftlint.yml` present) reports 38 `error`-level violations inside candidate files: `GitHubTransport.swift` snake_case DTO properties (`client_id`, `device_code`, `access_token`, …, plus `k`/`v` and one 209-char line) and `GitHubAuth+State+Reducer.swift` `reduce` cyclomatic complexity 21. The outcome claims \"lint 0 serious\" on 6 touched files; the reducer and transport files are part of the candidate. Either add `CodingKeys`/a checked-in `.swiftlint.yml` that documents the DTO exception, or state the exact bound with the count. Do not report a lint gate as clean when the tool reports errors.\n41|\n42|### Minor (not blocking, fix alongside F6 if cheap)\n43|- `selectInstallation`: `currentToken()` throwing `.revoked/.unauthorized/.tokenRefreshFailed` yields `syncFailed` while `refreshInstallations` yields `.failed(relogin)` for the same class; inconsistent user outcome for a revoked session.\n44|- `restoreSession`: a non-auth refresh failure (5xx/rate-limit on the token endpoint) followed by a 401 on `/user` with the expired access token deletes the still-valid refresh token. Consider treating a 401 right after an *unrefreshed expiring* token as \"retry later\", not revoke.\n45|- `UserDefaultsGitHubSessionIdentityStore` (production adapter) has no round-trip test; only the in-memory store is exercised.\n46|\n47|## Accepted as-is\n48|Device Flow transport and error mapping; cancellation (poll generation, code destroyed); 401→relogin / 403→stale with `.connected` preserved; no PAT UI, no `gh` import, PATGuard on all three call sites with negative tests; tokens absent from `GitHubAuth.State`/actions/logs; Keychain scoping and sweep; management window Container→Page composition dispatching production effects; menu keeps existing controls plus the settings entry; `.spec/` materialized with registration and removal in scope; generator-owned `Project.swift`.\n49|\n50|## AC-row status after review\n51|Producer table: 9 of 11 rows driven (rows 1 and 11 are stated bounds; row 1 build verified by me, row 11 menu wiring is manual/no UI tests). Row 7 (logout) is downgraded: driven for the sequential case only; the interleaved class fails (F6). All other driven rows hold under my reruns and the producer mutants.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c519","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a841-0b8e-7df2-8923-843adf19c894"},"sequence":231,"recorded_at":1780531400000457,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df"},"call_id":"call_01a0a84191d8766b87ad071cef9ff920","text":"Read text file `/tmp/RA.swift`.\n1|import Foundation\n2|import Testing\n3|import Relux\n4|@testable import RunnerControlCore\n5|\n6|/// Transport that delays every response so a logout can interleave with an in-flight call.\n7|actor SlowTransport: GitHubHTTPTransport {\n8|    private var queue: [GitHubHTTPResponse]\n9|    private(set) var requests: [GitHubHTTPRequest] = []\n10|    let delayMs: Int\n11|    init(_ responses: [GitHubHTTPResponse], delayMs: Int) { self.queue = responses; self.delayMs = delayMs }\n12|    func send(_ request: GitHubHTTPRequest) async throws -> GitHubHTTPResponse {\n13|        requests.append(request)\n14|        try? await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(delayMs))\n15|        guard !queue.isEmpty else { throw GitHubTransportError.invalidResponse }\n16|        return queue.removeFirst()\n17|    }\n18|}\n19|\n20|private func attackHarness(transport: any GitHubHTTPTransport, store: GitHubKeychainStore, identities: any GitHubSessionIdentityStoring) async -> (GitHubAuth.Flow, Relux.Testing.Logger) {\n21|    let logger = Relux.Testing.Logger()\n22|    let dispatcher = Relux.Dispatcher(logger: logger)\n23|    let flow = await GitHubAuth.Flow(\n24|        deviceFlow: GitHubDeviceFlow(transport: transport),\n25|        api: GitHubAPIClient(transport: transport),\n26|        refresher: GitHubTokenRefresh(transport: transport, store: store),\n27|        store: store, identityStore: identities,\n28|        configProvider: { _ in testConfig }, sleeper: { _ in }, dispatcher: dispatcher)\n29|    return (flow, logger)\n30|}\n31|\n32|private func names(_ logger: Relux.Testing.Logger) -> [String] {\n33|    logger.actions.compactMap { $0 as? GitHubAuth.Action }.map { String(describing: $0).components(separatedBy: \"(\")[0] }\n34|}\n35|\n36|// RA1: logout while restoreSession is awaiting /user must not revive the session afterwards.\n37|@Test func reviewerLogoutDuringRestoreDoesNotReviveSession() async throws {\n38|    let store = GitHubKeychainStore(backend: InMemoryKeychainBackend())\n39|    let identities = InMemoryGitHubSessionIdentityStore(value: GitHubSessionIdentity(serverHost: \"github.com\", userID: 42, clientID: testConfig.clientID, username: \"octo\"))\n40|    try await store.save(GitHubAuth.TokenRecord(accessToken: \"ghu_saved\", refreshToken: \"ghr_saved\", expiresAt: Date().addingTimeInterval(3600)), serverHost: \"github.com\", userID: 42, clientID: testConfig.clientID)\n41|    let transport = SlowTransport([\n42|        jsonResponse([\"login\": \"octo\", \"id\": 42]),\n43|        jsonResponse([\"installations\": []]),\n44|    ], delayMs: 300)\n45|    let (flow, logger) = await attackHarness(transport: transport, store: store, identities: identities)\n46|    let restore = Task { _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.restoreSession) }\n47|    try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(100))\n48|    _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.logout)\n49|    _ = await restore.value\n50|    try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(200))\n51|    let seq = names(logger)\n52|    print(\"RA1 sequence:\", seq)\n53|    let loggedOutIdx = seq.lastIndex(of: \"loggedOut\") ?? -1\n54|    let afterLogout = Array(seq.suffix(from: loggedOutIdx + 1))\n55|    #expect(!afterLogout.contains(\"connected\"), \"restore revived session after logout: \\(afterLogout)\")\n56|    #expect(!afterLogout.contains(\"accountVerified\"), \"restore verified account after logout: \\(afterLogout)\")\n57|    // Session must be gone: a sync now is a no-op.\n58|    let before = logger.actions.count\n59|    _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.refreshInstallations)\n60|    try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(100))\n61|    #expect(logger.actions.count == before, \"refresh after logout still had a session: \\(names(logger))\")\n62|    #expect(await identities.load() == nil)\n63|}\n64|\n65|// RA2: logout while refreshInstallations is awaiting /user/installations must not emit sync results afterwards.\n66|@Test func reviewerLogoutDuringRefreshDoesNotEmitSyncAfterLoggedOut() async throws {\n67|    let store = GitHubKeychainStore(backend: InMemoryKeychainBackend())\n68|    let identities = InMemoryGitHubSessionIdentityStore()\n69|    let transport = SlowTransport([\n70|        jsonResponse([\"device_code\": \"dev1\", \"user_code\": \"USER-1\", \"verification_uri\": \"https://github.com/login/device\", \"expires_in\": 900, \"interval\": 1]),\n71|        jsonResponse([\"access_token\": \"ghu_x\", \"refresh_token\": \"ghr_y\", \"expires_in\": 3600]),\n72|        jsonResponse([\"login\": \"octo\", \"id\": 42]),\n73|        jsonResponse([\"installations\": []]),\n74|        jsonResponse([\"installations\": [[\"id\": 7, \"account\": [\"login\": \"acme\", \"type\": \"Organization\"]]]]),\n75|    ], delayMs: 150)\n76|    let (flow, logger) = await attackHarness(transport: transport, store: store, identities: identities)\n77|    _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.beginLogin(serverHost: nil))\n78|    let deadline = ContinuousClock.now.advanced(by: .seconds(3))\n79|    while ContinuousClock.now < deadline, !names(logger).contains(\"connected\") { try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(20)) }\n80|    #expect(names(logger).contains(\"connected\"))\n81|    let refresh = Task { _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.refreshInstallations) }\n82|    try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(50))\n83|    _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.logout)\n84|    _ = await refresh.value\n85|    try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(100))\n86|    let seq = names(logger)\n87|    print(\"RA2 sequence:\", seq)\n88|    let loggedOutIdx = seq.lastIndex(of: \"loggedOut\") ?? -1\n89|    let afterLogout = Array(seq.suffix(from: loggedOutIdx + 1))\n90|    #expect(afterLogout.isEmpty, \"actions after loggedOut: \\(afterLogout)\")\n91|}\n92|\n93|// RA3: beginLogin while restoreSession is in flight must not have restore clobber the login state.\n94|@Test func reviewerLoginDuringRestoreIsNotClobberedByRestore() async throws {\n95|    let store = GitHubKeychainStore(backend: InMemoryKeychainBackend())\n96|    let identities = InMemoryGitHubSessionIdentityStore(value: GitHubSessionIdentity(serverHost: \"github.com\", userID: 42, clientID: testConfig.clientID, username: \"octo\"))\n97|    try await store.save(GitHubAuth.TokenRecord(accessToken: \"ghu_saved\", refreshToken: \"ghr_saved\", expiresAt: Date().addingTimeInterval(3600)), serverHost: \"github.com\", userID: 42, clientID: testConfig.clientID)\n98|    let transport = SlowTransport([\n99|        jsonResponse([\"login\": \"octo\", \"id\": 42]),                       // restore: /user (slow)\n100|        jsonResponse([\"device_code\": \"dev1\", \"user_code\": \"USER-1\", \"verification_uri\": \"https://github.com/login/device\", \"expires_in\": 900, \"interval\": 1]), // login: device code\n101|        jsonResponse([\"installations\": []]),                             // restore: installations\n102|        jsonResponse([\"error\": \"authorization_pending\"]),\n103|    ], delayMs: 200)\n104|    let (flow, logger) = await attackHarness(transport: transport, store: store, identities: identities)\n105|    let restore = Task { _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.restoreSession) }\n106|    try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(50))\n107|    _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.beginLogin(serverHost: nil))\n108|    _ = await restore.value\n109|    try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(600))\n110|    let seq = names(logger)\n111|    print(\"RA3 sequence:\", seq)\n112|    let codeIdx = seq.lastIndex(of: \"codeReceived\") ?? -1\n113|    let afterCode = Array(seq.suffix(from: codeIdx + 1)).filter { $0 == \"connected\" || $0 == \"accountVerified\" }\n114|    #expect(afterCode.isEmpty, \"restore emitted \\(afterCode) after login codeReceived\")\n115|    _ = await flow.apply(GitHubAuth.Effect.cancelLogin)\n116|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c51b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a841-0b8e-7df2-8923-843adf19c894"},"sequence":232,"recorded_at":1780531400000459,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df"},"call_id":"call_01a0a84192fa73ad81b008c9c15a4581","text":"Read text file `/tmp/outcome-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-97dhxd — rework rev2 outcome (review findings F1–F5)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review` via handoff).\n4|Candidate: uncommitted in Story worktree, branch tip unchanged at `7d2126a`.\n5|\n6|## F1 — session restore from Keychain (was: in-memory only)\n7|\n8|- New `GitHubSessionIdentityStore.swift`: non-secret identity\n9|  (`serverHost`, `userID`, `clientID`, `username`) in UserDefaults;\n10|  tokens stay in Keychain. In-memory store for tests.\n11|- New `GitHubAuth.Effect.restoreSession` + `Action.restoreStarted`\n12|  (reducer → existing `.verifyingAccount`; no UI change needed).\n13|  Flow loads identity → Keychain record → PAT-shape check →\n14|  opportunistic serialized refresh → `GET /user` validation →\n15|  installations (+ first-installation repositories) → `.connected`.\n16|- 401/revoked/`invalid_grant`/PAT-shaped store → clears Keychain +\n17|  identity, `.failed(relogin|none)`. Offline/403/rate-limit →\n18|  restored session with stale `syncFailed`; local control and logout\n19|  stay available. Missing Keychain record clears orphan identity.\n20|- `logout` also deletes identity, and reaches persisted stores via the\n21|  identity when the in-memory session is already gone (relaunch can\n22|  never orphan tokens).\n23|- Production call site: `AppRegistry.start()` dispatches\n24|  `.restoreSession` once after `RunnerRuntime.make`, before the loops,\n25|  so the 30 s GitHub loop sees `.connected`.\n26|- Spec: `.spec/github-login-device-flow.md` gains a Session restore section.\n27|\n28|## F2 — refresh concurrency at the production call site\n29|\n30|`GitHubAuth.Flow.currentToken()` (used by `.refreshInstallations` and\n31|`.selectInstallation`) is now driven directly: expiring token\n32|(`expiresAt` now+30 s) → one refresh POST observed in\n33|`TestTransport.requests` → stored token rotates → `syncSucceeded`;\n34|`invalid_grant` on refresh → `.failed(relogin)`; two concurrent Flow\n35|callers (`refreshInstallations` + `selectInstallation(7)`) coalesce to\n36|exactly one `refresh_token` grant (URL-routing test transport).\n37|\n38|## F3 — PAT guard on the refresh path\n39|\n40|`refreshRejectsFineGrainedPATWithoutSaving` feeds\n41|`{\"access_token\":\"github_pat_...\"}` to `GitHubTokenRefresh.refresh`,\n42|expects `.patNotSupported`, and proves the Keychain still holds the\n43|old `ghu_` token. All three `PATGuard` call sites now have negative tests.\n44|\n45|## F4 — audit wired; redaction bounded\n46|\n47|- `AppConfig.current(bundle:serverHost:)` now calls\n48|  `auditNoSecrets(in: bundle.infoDictionary)` first and fails closed.\n49|  `configAuditRunsThroughCurrentBundle` drives both branches through\n50|  `current(bundle:)` with real temp `.bundle` plists (tainted → \n51|  `.embeddedSecret(\"ClientSecret\")`; clean → loads).\n52|- `Redaction.sanitize` has no production caller: STATED BOUND.\n53|  No diagnostics export exists in this slice (log tail / `_diag`\n54|  lands with catalog/lifecycle); `RuntimeLogger` emits action types\n55|  only, so there is nothing to scrub. Noted in code + here.\n56|\n57|## F5 — public binding embedded via generator\n58|\n59|- `ios-app-manager.json`: `GitHubAppClientID: \"Iv23ligBUam7vZitsE1G\"`,\n60|  `GitHubAppSlug: \"relux-runner-control\"`, `marketing_version: \"1.2.0\"`.\n61|- Regenerated with `/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/work/ios-app-manager generate macos-app`\n62|  (exit 0, \"existing source files preserved\"). `Project.swift` diff is\n63|  exactly: version 1.2.0 + the two public keys. Never hand-edited.\n64|- Release `Info.plist` carries `GitHubAppClientID` /\n65|  `GitHubAppSlug`; plist + binary strings contain no\n66|  `secret`/`private_key`/`ghp_`/`github_pat_`/`ghu_`/`ghr_` material.\n67|  No installation IDs, accounts, users, orgs, or repos hardcoded.\n68|\n69|## Incidental (kept minimal)\n70|\n71|- `handlePollSuccess` split into `loadLoginRepositories` +\n72|  `loginInstallationsFailed` (identical dispatch order) to fix the\n73|  pre-existing `cyclomatic_complexity` lint error (22 → under 20).\n74|- Fixed pre-existing lint errors in touched test files\n75|  (`try!` → `try` / scoped disable, `a`/`b`/`v` renames).\n76|- New test `flowLoginPhase401DuringInstallationsRequiresRelogin`\n77|  closes the login-tail 401 branch the split touched.\n78|\n79|## AC coverage — 9 of 11 rows driven via committed tests\n80|\n81|| # | AC row | Named committed test(s) | Production call site |\n82||---|---|---|---|\n83|| 1 | App builds | BOUND (verified via `./Scripts/build.sh` below, not a unit test) | `tuist generate` → `xcodebuild -scheme RunnerControl` → `codesign --verify` |\n84|| 2 | Real login UI drives production services | `flowLoginSuccessDrivesProductionEffectsToConnected` (+ `flowLoginPersistsSessionIdentityForLaterRestore`; UI binding manual, no UI tests) | `ManagementWindowContainer.beginLogin → GitHubAuth.Effect.beginLogin → GitHubAuth.Flow.apply` |\n85|| 3 | Cancellation | `flowCancellationDestroysCodeAndStopsPoll`, `flowCancelWhileConnectedRestoresConnected` | `GitHubAuth.Flow.apply(.cancelLogin)` |\n86|| 4 | slow_down | `flowSlowDownIncreasesIntervalThenSucceeds`, `slowDownAddsFiveSeconds` | `GitHubDeviceFlow.pollOnce` + `nextInterval` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin)` |\n87|| 5 | Expired code | `flowExpiredCodeFailsWithNewCode` | `GitHubDeviceFlow.pollOnce` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin)` |\n88|| 6 | Refresh concurrency | `flowRefreshInstallationsRefreshesExpiringTokenViaProductionPath`, `flowConcurrentRefreshAndSelectCoalesceToSingleRefresh`, `flowRefreshInstallationsWithInvalidGrantDuringRefreshRequiresRelogin` (+ helper `refreshSavesAtomicallyAndCoalescesConcurrentCallers`) | `GitHubAuth.Flow.currentToken()` via `Flow.apply(.refreshInstallations)` / `.selectInstallation` |\n89|| 7 | Logout (+ F1 restore) | `flowRestoreSessionConnectsFromPersistedIdentityThenLogoutClearsBoth`, `flowRestoreSessionWithRevokedTokenRequiresReloginAndClearsStorage`, `flowRestoreSessionWithoutIdentityIsNoop`, `flowLogoutClearsKeychainAndStopsSync`, `githubReducerRestoreStartedShowsVerifyingAccount` | `GitHubAuth.Flow.apply(.restoreSession)` from `AppRegistry.start()`; `Flow.apply(.logout)` |\n90|| 8 | 401 | `flowLoginPhase401DuringInstallationsRequiresRelogin`, `flow401DuringRefreshRequiresRelogin`, `apiClientMaps401And403` | `GitHubAPIClient.*` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin/.refreshInstallations/.restoreSession)` |\n91|| 9 | 403 | `flow403DuringRefreshKeepsConnectedWithStaleError`, `apiClientMaps401And403` | `GitHubAPIClient.fetchInstallations` via `Flow.apply(.refreshInstallations)` |\n92|| 10 | No PAT fallback | `refreshRejectsFineGrainedPATWithoutSaving`, `patGuardRejectsClassicAndFineGrainedPAT`, `apiClientRefusesPATWithoutNetwork`, `devicePollRejectsPATShapedToken` | `GitHubAuth.PATGuard.validate` via device poll, API client, and token refresh |\n93|| 11 | Existing menu functional | BOUND (Runners suite green; menu UI wiring manual, no UI tests) | `RunnerContainer.change → Runners.Effect.setEnabled → Runners.Flow.apply` |\n94|\n95|## Validation (real exit codes)\n96|\n97|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` → exit 0, 56/56 passed.\n98|- Skill script `run-macos-package-tests.sh --package Packages/RunnerControlCore --output .temp/macos-tests` → exit 0, 56 passed.\n99|- `./Scripts/build.sh` (tuist generate + Release xcodebuild + codesign verify) → exit 0, BUILD SUCCEEDED.\n100|- `codesign --verify --deep --strict .temp/products/RunnerControl.app` → exit 0.\n101|- `swiftlint lint` on 6 touched files → exit 0, 0 serious (118 warnings, same baseline classes as rev1: line_length, trailing_comma).\n102|- Not run: `RUN_LAUNCH_AGENT_INTEGRATION=1` launchd integration (touches host launchd; default suite skips it), UI tests (forbidden), release/notary (other Story).\n103|\n104|## Narrowing mutant evidence, rev2 round (all killed, exit 1)\n105|\n106|| Mutant | Narrowing (what it admits) | Named test that fails | Result |\n107||---|---|---|---|\n108|| R1 (reviewer rerun) Flow refreshes only when `refreshToken == nil` | expiring refreshable token never refreshed | `flowRefreshInstallationsRefreshesExpiringTokenViaProductionPath`, `flowConcurrentRefreshAndSelectCoalesceToSingleRefresh` | KILLED (exit 1; 0 refresh grants, stored token stale, no `syncSucceeded`) |\n109|| R2 (reviewer rerun) refresh-path PAT check is `ghp_`-only | admits `github_pat_*` on refresh | `refreshRejectsFineGrainedPATWithoutSaving` | KILLED (exit 1; mutant saved the PAT, store no longer `ghu_old`) |\n110|| N1 restore 401 narrowed to stale | revoked token restores as connected instead of relogin+clear | `flowRestoreSessionWithRevokedTokenRequiresReloginAndClearsStorage` | KILLED (exit 1; got connected-path actions, not `.failed(relogin)`) |\n111|| N2 logout skips identity delete | identity survives logout | `flowRestoreSessionConnectsFromPersistedIdentityThenLogoutClearsBoth` | KILLED (exit 1; `identities.load() == nil` failed) |\n112|| N3 refresh threshold narrowed to already-expired | admits soon-expiring (now+30 s) without refresh | `flowRefreshInstallationsRefreshesExpiringTokenViaProductionPath` | KILLED (exit 1; 1 token POST not 2, stored token stale) |\n113|| W1 `current(bundle:)` skips audit call | admits embedded `ClientSecret` | `configAuditRunsThroughCurrentBundle` | KILLED (exit 1; admitted secret). Wiring proof; class coverage is M7 (rev1, accepted) |\n114|| L1 login-tail 401 narrowed to `.revoked`-only | login-phase 401 connects instead of relogin | `flowLoginPhase401DuringInstallationsRequiresRelogin` | KILLED (exit 1; got connected-path, not `.failed(relogin)`) |\n115|\n116|Rev1 mutants M1–M8, M9d were accepted by the reviewer (killed); M9/M9c\n117|survivors carry the accepted triple-redundancy bound on untouched\n118|cancellation code — not rerun. No new survivors in rev2.\n119|\n120|## Bounds restated\n121|\n122|- Tokens/`device_code` never in `GitHubAuth.State`, actions, logs, or\n123|  `RuntimeLogger` (type-only). Identity store holds no secrets.\n124|- Offline/403/rate-limit keep local control and the restored session;\n125|  401/revoked → relogin with storage cleared.\n126|- Enterprise hosts get host-scoped endpoints; per-server App\n127|  registration + Device Flow support still required (concrete error).\n128|- No `gh` import, no PAT UI, no client secret/private key anywhere.\n129|- Work left uncommitted in Story worktree; branch tip unchanged.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
