{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d1fd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a841-0b8e-7df2-8923-843adf19c894"},"sequence":1881,"recorded_at":1780531400003757,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0a9b0514-6796-4bae-973f-c687f7c4e3df"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Rework rev3 is ready for review (handed off to review, board status `to-review`).\n\nWhat changed: the F6 lifecycle race is fixed as a complete boundary — `beginLogin`/`cancelLogin`/`logout` bump the Flow generation and cancel the in-flight token refresh; `restoreSession`, `restoreInstallations`, `refreshInstallations`, `selectInstallation`, and `currentToken` capture the generation at entry and stop silently after every `await` once superseded (no state emission, no session/identity restore, no token saves). The refresh helper throws `CancellationError` at a pre-save check with post-save compare-and-delete. Also fixed locally: select-with-revoked-token now surfaces relogin like refresh, and a 401 after a transiently failed refresh keeps tokens and reports stale instead of deleting a valid refresh token.\n\nEvidence: RA1–RA3 committed verbatim — all three failed on the pre-fix candidate with the exact reviewer sequences and pass after; plus 5 new regressions (RA4 token-absence, helper cancel, 401 heuristic, select relogin, UserDefaults round-trip). Full suite 64/64 green (exit 0), Release build + strict codesign green, plist binding `Iv23ligBUam7vZitsE1G`/`relux-runner-control`/1.2.0 intact with zero secret keys. Narrowing mutants F6a/F6b/F6c each killed by their named test (exit 1), no new survivors. F7 resolved with the exact count: swiftlint default config exits 2 with 45 first-party errors, reported red as a bound (37 pre-existing DTO/reducer, 3 new from the required guard density, 5 pre-existing/earlier-rev) — no broad cleanup. AC 9 of 11 driven, row 7 upgraded to full interleaved coverage.\n\nCandidate left uncommitted at tip `7d2126a`; outcome attached as `TASK-260916-97dhxd_outcome-rev3.md`.","reason":null}}
